  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MozParks (previously named Beluluane Industrial Park or BIP) is a public private partnership between the Government of Mozambique (40%) and private Swiss-Mozambican investors (60%). Their mission is to support sustainable industrialization in Mozambique. MozParks has been implementing the Mimi Niko Kazi Youth Employment Programme and its predecessor, the overall goal of the project is to provide access to the employment market to young people by serving as bridge between young graduates and the private sector/industries</narrative>
  </description>
